<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:28Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Escalating conflict in Yemen as Houthis say seized new strategic area</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:649fce44ae1d8990b2791032a4f48536e08d7f8caa5df042bcaa824e3a250911</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T13:50:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261014-escalating-conflict-in-yemen-as-houthis-say-seized-new-strategic-area" /><summary type="html">The Iran-backed Houthi rebels in Yemen released footage said to show operations in the Taiz governorate. Fighting between the Houthis and forces loyal to Yemen’s internationally recognised government, backed by Saudi-Arabia, has escalated dramatically in recent weeks after the Houthis managed to seize a number of strategically important areas, according to reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Duane Davis sentenced to minimum 40 years for Tupac killing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ac7c537a76e33c7959d06cbac17c6dd4aa39244016d7d729ac1c4fea0294887f</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T13:48:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261014-duane-davis-sentenced-to-minimum-40-years-for-tupac-killing" /><summary type="html">Duane Davis, the former Los Angeles gang leader who boasted in books and interviews of his involvement in the killing of rapper Tupac Shakur, only to deny it when he came to trial, was sentenced to a minimum 40 years in prison on Tuesday. FRANCE 24's Wassim Cornet reports from Los Angeles, United States.</summary></entry><entry><title>Guillaume Canet and Marion Cotillard reunite on the silver screen in thriller 'Karma'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:523b31021cfa5739c6cd45e904cbed16b271efa2bd82e222de5242bc487c79f5</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T13:34:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261014-guillaume-canet-and-marion-cotillard-reunite-on-the-silver-screen-in-thriller-karma" /><summary type="html">This week on arts24, our French film critic Manon Kerjean covers thrillers, history, legend and animation. "Karma" reunites exes Guillaume Canet and Marion Cotillard on screen for a thriller about a woman fleeing her past and the cult she escaped. "Moulin" follows Resistance hero Jean Moulin's final days in captivity, while "Le Fantôme de l'Opéra" returns for a modern retelling, but do critics buy it? We also discuss "Iron Boy", Louis Clichy's animated coming-of-age story inspired by his own childhood.</summary><category term="arts24" /></entry><entry><title>French MPs back bill to tackle sexual and gender-based violence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a649592da7f98dd1294ac9041aef5faefa20981fd458a6967e3de5e65f0096ad</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T12:58:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20261014-french-mps-back-bill-to-tackle-sexual-and-gender-based-violence" /><summary type="html">In France, a child is reportedly raped or sexually assaulted every three minutes. In a bid to put an end to sexual and gender-based violence, French MPs have voted for a comprehensive bill that could turn into law by the end of the year; it has yet to be debated by the more conservative Senate at the end of the month. FRANCE 24's Aurore Dupuis, who made the documentary "Broken children", tells us how this new law could help improve the situation for women and children in France.</summary><category term="Entre Nous" /></entry><entry><title>Cheap weapons, growing fears: Inside the Taliban’s drone campaign against Pakistan</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5e06ff93695892931958007142a88ae8088a7c38a9bdc0ba827a92aa3a407112</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T12:52:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261014-taliban-suicide-drone-attacks-pakistan" /><summary type="html">Pakistan says it intercepted 23 suicide drones launched from Afghanistan into Pakistani airspace in September alone. Since the conflict began in February 2026, the Taliban have increasingly used drones to attack Pakistan, raising concerns in Islamabad.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Louvre boss warns of closure risk without major renovations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2d9c99731e57051986f440871b9574bc75bfb0a137ba707c1c798f29ac7d61ca</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T12:21:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/live-news/20261014-louvre-boss-warns-of-closure-risk-without-major-renovations" /><summary type="html">The Louvre Museum risks having to close its doors to the public unless lawmakers approve a major overhaul of the creaking and over-capacity institution, its head told a French newspaper on Wednesday.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump's crackdown on migrants: New documentary investigates ICE operations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3a723778582e5e9781adc83b0c20cc3f7c836ee2beebf5ff212d0e2db80f3c1e</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T11:51:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261014-trump-s-crackdown-on-migrants-new-documentary-investigates-ice-operations" /><summary type="html">A new documentary from our sister channel France Télévisions explores US President Donald Trump's relentless crackdown on immigration and the agency carrying it out – United States Immigration and Customs Enforcement, better known as ICE. "ICE : La chasse a l'homme", or "A Manhunt Named ICE" interviews agents and also some of the people who lives have been turned upside down by ICE operations. In Perspective, we spoke to the film's co-writer Marine Pradel.</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>French student protesters are being 'exploited' by political forces, Macron says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:118627b94e70986df9ee1da69593a47f1a74536fe6cace532b2cae22ec8b9892</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T11:33:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261014-macron-says-french-student-protesters-exploited-by-political-forces" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron said on Wednesday that France's student protesters are being "exploited" by political forces ahead of the country's presidential election in April 2027. Hard-left candidate Jean-Luc Melenchon participated in a Paris demonstration while hard-right frontrunner Marine Le Pen voiced support for the police deployed to protests.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>Republicans weigh midterms strategy, pour money into campaigns even in red states</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0587f34162c0a344bf5e72c491646e4c9d6ee902e3ebbb24dfacb90124b718e1</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T10:56:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261014-republicans-weigh-midterms-strategy-pour-money-into-campaigns-even-in-red-states" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump said Tuesday Republicans face an equally difficult fight to retain control of the House of Representatives and the Senate in November's midterm elections, despite forecasts suggesting a considerably tougher contest in the House. Yet the party is pouring hundreds of millions of dollars into defending congressional and state-level seats once considered safely red. In some states, notably North Carolina and Georgia, they appear to be scaling back their ambitions – shifting resources to other Republican strongholds where Democrats are mounting unexpected challenges, as FRANCE 24's International Affairs Commentator Douglas Herbert explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>Faithful pray for Pope Leo after lung cancer diagnosis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5920340e2d547e4aa683ce502be3fc9eb36ba9b9b0a60c1eda9eeebcbfb560c5</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T10:55:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261014-faithful-pray-for-pope-leo-after-lung-cancer-diagnosis" /><summary type="html">World leaders, Catholics across the globe and senior cardinals at the Vatican offered prayers for Pope Leo on Wednesday after doctors announced the 71-year-old pontiff had been diagnosed with lung cancer and had part of one lung removed. The cancer diagnosis ​for a pope known ‌to be relatively young and energetic and who was elected only in May 2025 caused shock.</summary></entry><entry><title>Dangote refinery extends IPO: Plant has reshaped Nigeria's fuel market</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:078ac0e0acbd9664a1552433d584701739f413013218b9906d66800e8f8e3867</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T10:53:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261014-dangote-refinery-extends-ipo-plant-has-reshaped-nigeria-s-fuel-market" /><summary type="html">There has been a huge popular success for the IPO of the Dangote Refinery now ending on October 27th, 2026, after a 2-week extension. With the escalation of the conflict in the Middle East, the closure of the Strait of Hormuz has caused a surge in global crude prices and, in turn, supply shortages – pushing African and European countries to turn in mass to the Dangote refinery. The leading African producer of crude oil seeks to transform its status to a regional hub for refining and petrochemicals. FRANCE 24's Chinwe Ossundu reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>F1, Rwanda announce creation of African Grand Prix</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6b53e3c17ff95c9bf89b9bf92b482de4870e06b7e9d033070f63fd5b5e4ad651</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T10:51:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261014-f1-rwanda-announce-creation-of-african-grand-prix" /><summary type="html">Rwanda will host Africa's first Formula One Grand Prix since 1993 in "the early 2030s" after the circuit announced a decade-long deal with the country on Tuesday. The East African nation has been chasing a Grand Prix race for years, having already used football, basketball and other sports to enhance its image and attract investment. Human rights campaigners Amnesty International ⁠accused Formula One ​of offering Rwanda a "sportswashing prize".</summary></entry><entry><title>'Super-Earths' might be better than our planet. But are they reachable?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a5f662e506c37a620ecf17ada4bfcbd7299d2598177aadff868017108422a103</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T09:57:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261014-super-earths-might-be-better-than-our-planet-but-are-they-reachable" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Wednesday, October 14: Portuguese papers are discussing the country's housing problems. Next: in Germany, a humanoid robot has sexually assaulted a teenage girl. In science news, there might be planets more habitable than Earth out there. Finally, Cosmopolitan helps us find out if we are dating a loser.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>A bear with a taste for honey: Winnie the Pooh turns 100</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:792c6b3ca7a8e881126a9cb0946442cbb801cba8b5d68df14f0ada60d5c35418</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T09:48:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261014-a-bear-with-a-taste-for-honey-winnie-the-pooh-turns-100" /><summary type="html">The world's most famous and very greedy bear is celebrating his centenary this year. Winnie the Pooh made his debut in a story called "The Wrong Kind of Bees" in the London Evening News. The first collection of stories, illustrated by E. H. Shepard, was published as a book on October 14, 1926.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukrainian ex-officer stands trial in Germany over Nord Stream bombing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4c6c1b2f9b4a96470348656e5267fd2e60e35c40c9dc026c3a38ac1870066c44</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T09:45:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261014-ukrainian-ex-officer-stands-trial-in-germany-over-nord-stream-bombing" /><summary type="html">A Ukrainian ex-military officer goes on trial in Germany on Wednesday, accused of organising the secret operation ​that blew up the Nord Stream gas pipelines in September 2022, severing western Europe from the biggest source of Russian natural gas. The suspect, identified under German privacy rules only as Serhii K., is accused of leading a group of Ukrainian agents including divers and an explosives expert to mount one of the biggest infrastructure sabotage operations of modern times. FRANCE 24's Jörg Taszman reports from Berlin, Germany.</summary></entry><entry><title>Spanish royals make sensitive official visit to sensitive Ceuta enclave</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0b2b66c1b1ad0c9693b68ded1bc68dead229ff65cf7b682a2d8bcd97cbebe6be</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T09:43:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261014-spanish-royals-make-sensitive-official-visit-to-sensitive-ceuta-enclave" /><summary type="html">Cheering crowds waving Spanish flags filled Ceuta on Tuesday as King Felipe VI and Queen Letizia made a diplomatically sensitive visit to the city following July's migrant influx from Morocco. Their trip is the first royal visit since 2007, when a diplomatic crisis erupted with neighbouring Morocco, which claims sovereignty over Ceuta and Spain's other North African territory of Melilla.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukraine reports Russian attacks with no warnings, Trump says US still sharing intel</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a443858749457a21155fbcd7a4b29a30fa594b5a88e52c793044ce45557a8822</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T09:41:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261014-ukraine-reports-russian-attacks-with-no-warnings-trump-says-us-still-sharing-intel" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump said on Tuesday that Washington was still sharing intelligence ​with Ukraine, even as Kyiv reported new Russian missile attacks that came without usual warnings and accused Russia of violating an energy truce the US president announced at the weekend. Kyiv relies heavily on US intelligence for early warnings of missile strikes and for its own targeting of Russian military sites, experts and officials say.</summary></entry><entry><title>French protests enter 4th week: Demonstrations backing students gather strength</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:225b9f53218157005072ea844c9e53fe6dec57efd00de402334fce53e4e65a47</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T09:40:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261014-french-protests-enter-4th-week-demonstrations-backing-students-gather-strength" /><summary type="html">Tens of thousands of people joined rallies across France on Tuesday to support protesting high school students demanding better conditions in a major challenge to President Emmanuel Macron as his term winds down.  French students say they are determined to press their demands over absent teachers, dilapidated buildings, overcrowded schedules and other grievances. FRANCE 24's Clovis Casali reports from a high school in central Paris.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ex-gang leader sentenced to minimum 40 years for Tupac murder</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:023d00c7081c9f5d502637dba5f2e03ffd9af00d3f310686d1b8efcf46437e39</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T09:39:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261014-ex-gang-leader-sentenced-to-minimum-40-years-for-tupac-murder" /><summary type="html">Duane "Keffe D" Davis, the former Los Angeles gang leader who boasted for years of his involvement in the killing of rapper Tupac Shakur, only to deny it when he came to trial, was sentenced to a minimum 40 years in prison on Tuesday. The sentence, which will likely see him die in custody, comes three decades after the gunning down of one of the most influential hip hop artists of the late 20th century, and after years of criticism over investigations that went nowhere.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump fires Greece ambassador Guilfoyle over ethics scandal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ce506e4dda23ff2e0d47287d325aaf476d33539de632e28e24458ccbecc72dcb</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T09:35:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261014-trump-fires-greece-ambassador-guilfoyle-over-ethics-scandal" /><summary type="html">The White House said on Tuesday it had asked US Ambassador to Greece Kimberly Guilfoyle to resign after a series of news reports raised concerns she sold access to Trump administration officials in exchange for money, gifts and favors. US President Donald Trump had said on Monday that he ​was considering firing Guilfoyle, ‌who was once engaged to his son Donald Trump Jr.  FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Rochelle Ferguson Bouyahi tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Pope Leo XIV recovering after lung cancer operation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:14cc625e3305eac9829704dac219e63399c8c1d63b05392632807d49c1af505e</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T09:33:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261014-pope-leo-xiv-recovering-after-lung-cancer-operation" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo XIV spent a calm night and was to begin post-surgery recovery Wednesday, a day after having a cancerous tumour removed from his lung. Part of the pope's right lung was removed in the operation and the leader of the world's 1.4 billion Catholics is awaiting the results of tests to determine if the cancer has spread. FRANCE 24's Seema Gupta reports from Rome, Italy.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nvidia's Huang announces new investments in French tech sector</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a72d03ab615936385e9f35449f169716436b3516b99c1f02860ef1d728204b9f</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T09:29:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20261014-nvidia-s-huang-announces-new-investments-in-french-tech-sector" /><summary type="html">Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang stops by Paris to tout new stakes in French AI-enabled tech firms like medical booking site Doctolib. Also in this edition: OpenAI says it caught a spy red-handed, and China's trade surplus continues to boom despite soaring energy costs and trade conflicts.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine says Starlink restricted operations overnight, disrupting military missions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:95ea2806dee7656f46be0e0605bbe36165352b3256e415138113a860916e2b2f</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T09:14:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261014-ukraine-says-starlink-restricted-operations-overnight-disrupting-military-missions" /><summary type="html">Elon Musk's Starlink imposed restrictions on the operation of internet terminals in Ukraine overnight, disrupting military missions, an adviser to the Ukrainian president said on Wednesday. The official said Ukraine was given no prior warning about the restrictions to the satellite system it relies on for battlefield operations.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>‘Dark day for Turkey’: Pro-opposition TV channel boss slams police raid, broadcast halt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0de070d7c659a7c7e08fffe5dfa7fac5ca7edf09ef3319ab417e65ffe5231ba4</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T09:09:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261014-dark-day-for-turkey-pro-opposition-tv-channel-boss-slams-police-raid-broadcast-halt" /><summary type="html">Turkish authorities appointed a government trustee to run popular broadcaster Halk TV on Wednesday after police raided its headquarters, halting live broadcasts and arresting 11 people. Halk chairman Cafer Mahirogluin denounced "a dark day for Turkey", adding that seven of his family members were among those detained.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry></feed>
